{"OptimizedCursorPaginator passes negative cursor.offset directly to Django queryset slicing, but Django raises AssertionError for negative slice indices despite the comment claiming Django handles negative slicing": 0.9650771617889404, "OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key calls math.floor()/math.ceil() directly on datetime objects from AuditLogEntry, which raises TypeError since math.floor() doesn't work on datetime objects": 0.9837796092033386, "OptimizedCursorPaginator.value_from_cursor returns raw cursor value without converting back to datetime, causing invalid SQL when comparing a number to a DateTimeField on subsequent pages": 0.9912354946136475, "The comment about negative offset handling being for 'authorized administrators' is misleading since has_global_access defaults to True for all org members, exposing the buggy paginator to more users than intended": 0.36848628520965576, "Users with org:write scope can trigger a 500 error by crafting a cursor with negative offset (e.g., '0:-5:0'), creating a denial-of-service vector for the audit logs feature": 0.8538740277290344}